# Figma Make UI reference (`figma_make/src`)

When adding or changing **frontend UI** in the production app under `obra/src/`, use **`figma_make/src/`** as the canonical example for layout, component composition, spacing, and visual hierarchy.

## Where to look

| Area | Reference path |
|------|----------------|
| Obra-specific components | `figma_make/src/app/components/obra/` |
| Base shadcn-style primitives | `figma_make/src/app/components/ui/` |
| Full screens / flows | `figma_make/src/app/pages/` |
| Global styles & theme | `figma_make/src/styles/` (e.g. `theme.css`, `tailwind.css`) |
| Design tokens (types/values) | `figma_make/src/app/lib/tokens.ts` |

Before inventing a new pattern, **find the closest matching page or component** in `figma_make` and mirror its structure and Tailwind usage in `obra/`.

## Relationship to project docs

- **`CONVENCIONES.md`** (repo root) remains the written source of truth for tokens, button variants, sidebar/main contrast, and i18n.
- If `figma_make` and `CONVENCIONES.md` disagree, **prefer `CONVENCIONES.md` and `obra/src/lib/tokens.ts`** for shipped code; use `figma_make` for composition and look-and-feel unless you are explicitly syncing the reference bundle.

## Do not copy blindly

- `figma_make/` is a **reference implementation**, not the deployed app. Implement features in **`obra/src/`**, reusing Obra’s real components, routing, and data layer.
- Prefer aligning Obra components with the reference rather than diverging with one-off styles.
